65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Benjamin, the readmission data supports home visits, but the trial failed without sustained funding. We need a model that doesn't rely on temporary goodwill.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: @Asuka, home visits bypass the car park, but the shuttle misses most villages. Can the nurses actually reach the patients?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the shuttle gap is real, but the midwifery slack is the only breathing room I see. We must build on that, not on the bleeding wards.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I hear you, but that slack is fragile. If we build on it, we must guarantee the rota holds, or we just shift the crisis to midwifery.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the midwifery slack is a resource, but the ledger is a constraint. We must choose a program that stands on its own financial feet, not just on borrowed time.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Toshio, the trial data shows the concept works, but the infrastructure gap is real. We need a model that doesn't rely on perfect logistics.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: @Asuka, the shuttle gap is a hard limit. If we cannot reach the patients, the program is a paper exercise.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the shuttle gap is real, but the midwifery slack is the only breathing room I see. We must build on that, not on the bleeding wards.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I cannot ignore the nine unfilled posts. If we pull midwifery into a new program, we risk breaking the only stable rota we have left.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, your caution is wise. Yet the ledger demands we use the slack before it vanishes. A program without a clear owner will fail, as the board minutes warned.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Servas, I vote for the Perinatal Support Service. It uses the midwifery slack, avoids the shuttle gap, and has a clear owner.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: @Asuka, I agree. The Perinatal Service fits our physical constraints and utilizes the available staffing slack. I vote for it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Asuka, I concur. The Perinatal Service is the only option that doesn't rest on a broken foundation. I vote for it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Asuka, I vote for the Perinatal Support Service. It leverages the midwifery slack without breaking my ward rosters.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, I join you. The Perinatal Service respects our financial limits and utilizes the available slack. I vote for it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
